Mak3P $version | Linux x86-64 Full
================================

Mak3P is a free, portable app for converting local audio to MP3, including audio tracks in supported video files. It works offline and this package includes FFmpeg and ffprobe.

Requirements
------------
Ubuntu 24.04 LTS x86-64 is the supported build baseline. Other distributions require glibc 2.39 or later, libstdc++ with GLIBCXX_3.4.32, and the X11, Xft, Fontconfig, and libpng runtime libraries. A graphical session with X11 or XWayland is required. ARM and musl-based distributions are not supported by this archive.

On Ubuntu 24.04, install missing desktop libraries with:
  sudo apt install libx11-6 libxinerama1 libxfixes3 libxcursor1 libxrender1 libxft2 libfontconfig1 libpng16-16t64 libstdc++6

Get started
-----------
1. Extract the archive to a writable Linux folder, keeping bin and documents beside Mak3P:
     tar -xzf Mak3P-v$version-linux-x64-full.tar.gz
2. Open a terminal in the extracted Mak3P folder and run:
     ./Mak3P
   Some file managers also allow double-clicking the executable. If executable permissions were lost while copying, run:
     chmod +x Mak3P bin/ffmpeg bin/ffprobe
3. Choose Add files to select files or folders, or drag them onto the window.
4. Choose a bitrate and Stereo, Mono, or Auto. Defaults are 320 kbps and Stereo. Under Output location, save beside each source or choose one writable folder for the entire batch.
5. Click Start conversion. Hover over a row or status for details. Cancel conversion stops unfinished work and keeps completed MP3s.

Mak3P supports FLAC, APE, WavPack, WAV, AIFF, AAC or ALAC in MP4/M4A, DSF, Ogg/Vorbis, Opus, WMA, AC-3, and MP3. It preserves supported tags and artwork. Hybrid WavPack conversion uses the .wv stream without applying .wvc correction files.

Source files stay intact. Existing output names receive numbered suffixes. Lower-bitrate sources use a supported bitrate at or below the target unless you enable Force upsampling. An MP3 that already matches the target can be skipped. Include MP3 from folders controls folder imports.

Help and licenses
-----------------
Open Mak3P > Help for the full guide. Keep both audio tools in bin. If they cannot start, check the requirements above and extract the entire archive again, then choose Retry.

Enable Write log file for a report beside the application. Review filenames, paths, and other personal information before sharing logs.

See LICENSES.txt for the Mak3P agreement and third-party notices. In the app, open Mak3P > About > License.

Report issues at https://github.com/Eager1Beaver/mak3p.
